-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 5, §5.12 מורה -יועץ
-- The middle-school counsellor: the goals and functions the pedagogical
-- secretariat approved; work unit, licensing, allowance and organisation
-- are pointers to section 3.12 and 1.12.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `5.12 מורה -יועץ`

@desc One goal or function of the counsellor, as the approved list states it.
DECLARE `counselling function` HAS
    `area of the function` IS A STRING
    `what the function is` IS A STRING

DECLARE `counsellor action` IS ONE OF
    `disclose information about a pupil who was in treatment`
    `interview most pupils personally`
    `respond to a pupil who turned to the counsellor`

§§ `5.12.1 יחידת עבודה`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_1/p1 A pure pointer: the work unit is section 3.12.1's, encoded there.

§§ `5.12.2 הסמכה`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_2/p1 A pure pointer: licensing is section 3.12.2's rules for counselling licences, encoded there.

§§ `5.12.3 הגדרת תפקידים`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p1 The opening words: the pedagogical secretariat approved the functions that follow.

-- ¶3: the counsellor pursues these goals "together with the homeroom
-- teacher and the school staff".
@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p3
`the goals of counselling` MEANS
    LIST
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p2 The heading of the goals ("מטרות היעוץ").
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p4
        -- Goal 1: conditions and a climate in which pupils develop by ability and inclination.
        `counselling function` "goal" "fostering conditions and a climate in which pupils develop by their ability and inclination, in study, society and emotional life",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p5
        -- Goal 2: awareness of individual needs and of the age's social and emotional problems.
        `counselling function` "goal" "developing awareness of individual needs, of the social and emotional problems typical of the pupils' age and of special needs of individuals and groups",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p6
        -- Goal 3: counselling the system on study and social frameworks.
        `counselling function` "goal" "counselling the system on conditions and frameworks that let pupils realise their ability",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p7
        -- Goal 4: help to pupils who struggle to adjust, counselling their teachers and parents.
        `counselling function` "goal" "helping pupils who struggle to adjust, and counselling their teachers and parents",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p8
        -- Goal 5: help to all pupils adjusting to new frameworks.
        `counselling function` "goal" "helping all pupils adjust to new study and social frameworks",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p9
        -- Goal 6: a counselling process toward self-knowledge for choices of study and work.
        `counselling function` "goal" "developing a counselling process by which the individual comes to know himself, as ground for choosing study and work"

-- The functions of the middle-school counsellor (¶10). Each row is one
-- function.
@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p10
`the functions of the middle-school counsellor` MEANS
    LIST
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p11 Heading of function group 1 (information, diagnosis and treatment).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p12
        -- 1(a) contact with the homeroom teachers and the treating staff of the feeding schools.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "keeping contact with homeroom teachers and the treating staff of the feeding schools",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p14
        -- 1(c) gathering the information on pupils and interpreting it.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "gathering the information on the pupils, summarising it and interpreting results",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p15
        -- 1(d) close contact with the psychological, medical, social and community services.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "keeping close contact with the psychological, medical, social and community services",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p16
        -- 1(e) regular meetings with the homeroom teacher to diagnose problems.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "helping the homeroom teacher in regular meetings to diagnose individual and class problems and seek solutions",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p17
        -- 1(f) planned class or group work on counselling topics.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "planned, continuous class or group work on counselling topics",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p19
        -- 1(h) finding adjustment problems and gathering the information on them.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "finding adjustment problems and gathering the information on them",
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p20
        -- 1(i) short supportive treatment of individuals, at the counsellor's professional judgement.
        `counselling function` "information, diagnosis and treatment" "short supportive treatment of individuals, by the counsellor's professional judgement and skills",
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p21 Heading of function 2 (counselling on class composition and placement).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p22
        -- 2: an active partner in dividing pupils into classes and groups.
        `counselling function` "class composition and placement" "an active partner in dividing the pupils into classes and groups",
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p23 Heading of function 3 (pupil mobility).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p24
        -- 3: taking part in directing each pupil to a fitting place, before the responsible committee.
        `counselling function` "pupil mobility" "taking part in directing the pupil to groups, tracks, electives and clubs by bringing information and considerations before the responsible committee",
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p25 Heading of function 4 (follow-up).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p26
        -- 4: following up graduates in their new frameworks.
        `counselling function` "follow-up" "following up the integration in study or work of pupils who finished the middle school",
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p27 Heading of function 5 (the interdisciplinary team).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p28
        -- 5: gathering the team's material and following up its recommendations.
        `counselling function` "the interdisciplinary team" "gathering the material brought before the interdisciplinary team and following up its recommendations",
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p29 Heading of function 6 (initiative).
        @ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p30
        -- 6: initiating further activities to advance the pupils.
        `counselling function` "initiative" "initiating further special activities to advance the pupils, using the resources of the school and the community"

-- 1(b): beyond the information passed on about all pupils, the counsellor
-- receives information on pupils who were in treatment, and it is
-- confidential: the counsellor SHANT disclose it. (When disclosure is
-- allowed is not said here; section 3.12.3's confidentiality rules are the
-- takanon's general ones.)
@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p13
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `counsellor action`
DECIDE `confidentiality of treated pupils' information` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `disclose information about a pupil who was in treatment`

-- 1(b)'s first sentence: besides what is passed on about all pupils, the
-- counsellor is given information on pupils who were in treatment, in the
-- school or outside it. Who passes it is not said.
`the counsellor is given information on pupils who were in treatment, in school or outside it` MEANS TRUE

-- 1(g): a personal interview with most pupils at least once a year (time
-- in school months), and answering pupils who turn to the counsellor.
@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p18
GIVEN `pupils interviewed this year` IS A NUMBER, `pupils in the school` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `most pupils were interviewed this year` `pupils interviewed this year` `pupils in the school` IF
    `pupils interviewed this year` GREATER THAN `pupils in the school` DIVIDED BY 2

@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p18
GIVEN `a pupil turned to the counsellor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `counsellor action`
DECIDE `interviews and open door` `a pupil turned to the counsellor` IS
    (PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `interview most pupils personally` WITHIN 12)
    RAND
    (IF `a pupil turned to the counsellor`
     THEN PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `respond to a pupil who turned to the counsellor`
     ELSE FULFILLED)

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p31 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_3/p32 Source (אסמכתא): a Director-General's circular.

§§ `5.12.6 גמול ייעוץ`

@ref akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_6/p1
GIVEN `serves as a middle-school counsellor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the counselling allowance` `serves as a middle-school counsellor` IF
    `serves as a middle-school counsellor`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_6/p2 A pointer: the allowance's terms are section 1.12's, encoded there.

§§ `5.12.7 המסגרת הארגונית`

-- akn:chp_5__sec_5_12__ssec_5_12_7/p1 A pure pointer: the organisational framework is section 3.12.7's, encoded there.

#ASSERT count `the goals of counselling` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count `the functions of the middle-school counsellor` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `most pupils were interviewed this year` 301 600
#TRACE `confidentiality of treated pupils' information` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `disclose information about a pupil who was in treatment` AT 3
